# breaks: ActiveHasDirectory INVARIANT nocrash
# code: workspace/reclaim.rs puts a workspace an earlier reclaim left
# `releasing` back to `active` before reclaiming it again (#229's
# finish_going_back, #311): when begin_reclaim then fails, a workspace
# torn down by the earlier reclaim is `active`.
<<<
    /\ \/ Fail /\ Exit(p)
       \/ Goto(p, "final") /\ UNCHANGED <<lock, failLeft>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<up, dbState, lease, entry, disk, leftReleasing, env, crashLeft,
                   quiesceLeft>>
===
    /\ \/ Fail /\ Exit(p) /\ UNCHANGED <<dbState, mem>>
       \/ dbState' = "active" /\ mem' = "active" /\ Goto(p, "check")
          /\ UNCHANGED <<lock, failLeft>>
    /\ UNCHANGED <<up, lease, loaded, handle, tracked, disk, leftReleasing, env,
                   crashLeft, quiesceLeft>>
>>>
